  "theorem": "The complete 50-dimensional PSp(4,3)-equivariant quadratic Hom space from the signed-edge 90 carries the phase-outer S3 action 16*trivial + 16*sign + 9*standard. Its symmetric part is 13*trivial + 3*sign + 5*standard, while its alternating part is 3*trivial + 13*sign + 4*standard. The equality of trivial and sign multiplicities forces the outer split 25+25; the nine standard copies give the 18-dimensional rotating phase sector.",
  "boundary": "This is an exact representation-theoretic decomposition of equivariant quadratic maps. It does not make the 50 basis maps physical couplings, identify the multiplicities 16 or 9 with unrelated W33 counts, or select a physical family or chirality.",
